WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:05.310
North Entrance
Ticketing

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.770
Good morning, Master.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.730
Hey, Mob. A bit chilly out today, isn't it?

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.180
Looks like you're all set, Ritsu.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.190
Didn't know you were so excited
about hot springs.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.180
This is nothing, really.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.700
Anyway, thanks for inviting me 
along as well, I guess...

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.410
You could at least <i>try</i> to 
sound like you mean it.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.620
Good morning, everyone.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.360
Hey, Serizawa.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.820
Uh, how long do you think this trip is?

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.510
We're staying one night. Just one.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.800
Oh, sorry...

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.260
I figured I'd bring some stuff just in case, 
and now here I am.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.970
And why do you look so beat
when we haven't even started the trip?

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.450
Well, I was so anxious last night 
that I couldn't sleep a wink.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.440
I haven't gone on holiday 
in twenty years...

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.920
I totally understand.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.090
I'd have trouble sleeping on the nights
before field trips, too.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.910
Ahem! Listen up, all of you.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:59.550
While this is a trip to the hot springs,
we're going for work.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.570
And you, Serizawa!

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.870
You're still a trainee!

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.830
Don't get too excited.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.510
Y-Yes, sir! I'm terribly sorry!

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.780
Now start handing these out.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.010
The First Spirits and Such Company Trip
 <b>~A Journey that Mends the Heart and Heals the Soul~</b>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.010
<b>Trip guide
</b>Date: 1/7
Published by: Spirits and Such Consultation Office

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.570
Wh-What is this?

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.440
Our trip guide.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.700
<i>You're</i> the most excited one here.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.560
Spirits and Such Consultation Office

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.560
<b>Two
Days
Ago</b>

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:23.560
Ibogami Hot Springs? 
I'm afraid I've never heard of it.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.110
Ibogami Hot Springs can be found deep 
in the mountains of Zebra Prefecture.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:28.520
Some might say it's a hidden gem.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:32.630
My family runs an inn there
that's been in business for a century.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.870
We were quite popular with 
hot springs enthusiasts,

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:40.410
but lately, because of some reviews,
 our business has tanked.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.150
Ah...

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.790
<b>Ibogami Hot Springs Reviews

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:45.790
I see... A parallel world, eh?

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.250
At first, I just thought someone 
had a grudge against us.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.460
But when guests would show up at our inn,

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:55.210
so many of them seemed completely exhausted.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.970
They all claimed that
they wandered into a parallel world.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.430
Oh, I'm terribly sorry.
 I caught a cold recently...

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.640
If this keeps up, our inn will be finished.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.350
Please help us, Master Reigen.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.200
<i>Ibogami Village in Zebra Prefecture, huh?</i>

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.740
<i>That's pretty far.</i>

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:17.190
<i>Plus, they might just be trying
to make themselves feel better</i>

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.530
<i>by blaming a "parallel world"
for their falling popularity.</i>

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.990
Of course, we'll pay for your
travel expenses along with your fee.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:27.140
And we'll provide accommodations
at our inn as well.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.900
We'll welcome you with open arms

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.960
and serve you dinner with 
nothing but local ingredients.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.250
How many people can I take with me?

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.210
Huh?

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.570
Ah, well... Ahem.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.130
Very well.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.220
I, Reigen Arataka, shall accept this job!

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.970
<b>Mob Psycho</b>

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.970
m 0 0 l -1 -1 l -1 -10 l 6 -17 l 11 -17 l 18 -10 l 18 -1 l 17 0

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.970
\hFirst\h
Spirits and Such
Company Trip

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.970
~<b>A Journey that Mends the Heart and Heals the Soul</b>~

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.480
<b>Hometown Shop</b>

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.610
<b>Zebra
Meigetsu</b>

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.870
Hey, this mountain veggie bento is great!

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:13.750
I'm pretty sure you bought too much.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.470
Well, she said she'd pay for 
all our travel expenses, so why not?

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.880
You're such a trashy bastard.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.640
Come on, loosen up already, Serizawa.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.980
Y-Yes, sir.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.270
But I'm still just a trainee...

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.110
I know what I said earlier,

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.640
but this trip is also a way
to welcome you to the company.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.650
You don't have to worry about 
doing anything this trip.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.030
You just need to carefully watch us work.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.620
Yes, sir...

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.480
Go on, have one. They're great.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.040
Things not to do list 1
•Do not turn down anything your boss offers you!!
•Do not sleep while working
•No being late!

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.700
In that case... I'll gratefully take one.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.530
This seems like a school trip, 
so it's pretty fun.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.170
Right, Nii-san?

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:57.670
Yeah.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.730
A school trip, huh? That takes me back.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:03.550
Playing cards, having pillow fights, 
testing everyone's courage...

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.610
I don't mind setting up
a test of courage tonight, you know?

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:10.240
Give me a break. We're not in grade school.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:22.280
I'm gonna run to the restroom.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.470
Oh, me too. 
I've been holding it for a while now.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:27.030
Then you can use it first, Nii-san.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:28.080
Let's go.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.750
Now that my belly's full, I'm getting sleepy.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.290
Wake me up when we get there.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.600
Y-Yes, sir!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.370
<b>Ibogami Tunnel</b>

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:20.750
Damn it, Serizawa.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.630
I told you to wake me up.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:28.170
Huh?

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.460
Ow, ow, ow...

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:38.520
<i>Ah, I see... This must be Mob's doing.</i>

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:43.840
I'm so sorry! You told me to 
wake you up, but I fell asleep!

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.970
What in the world is this?

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:50.100
Welp, guess it's time to reveal the trick.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.700
Hey, Mob. Quit hiding and come out.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.580
Did you really think something 
like this would scare me?

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:59.080
Dimple put you up to it, didn't he?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.710
He was talking about
a test of courage earlier.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:06.090
That's enough now. You're such a kid.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:13.650
Huh? Wait, I went that way, right?

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:15.140
What the heck are you doing here?

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.480
Well, uh...

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.760
Really? You're in cahoots with them, too?

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:19.670
No, I—

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:23.120
Yeah, yeah, I got it. Don't worry.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.840
You don't have to say a thing.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.530
Jeez...

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:30.700
Don't underestimate how smart
us adults can be...

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.330
Things not to do list 2
•When the boss makes a move,
"Wait and watch."
•The first 15 seconds are key
to making a good first impression!

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.080
Um, Reigen-san...

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:49.090
Yeah?! What's up, Serizawa?

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:53.140
I'm pretty sure this is the parallel world
the matron mentioned.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:01.440
Precisely. Excellent observation.

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:05.820
You get points for staying alert
even on vacation.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.130
Th... Thank you!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.200
<b>No signal</b>

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:18.370
<i>Next is our last stop, Ibogami Hot Springs. 
Ibogami Hot Springs.</i>

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.210
Nothing weird even happened.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.050
Reigen-san and Serizawa-san didn't wake up.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.940
They must be really tired.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.330
Hey.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:34.480
I've been waiting for you guys.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:35.650
Hanazawa-kun.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:36.970
You're rather early.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:41.680
Since you were kind enough to invite me,
I thought I'd scout the area first.

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.580
Those two are fast asleep.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.080
I wanted to thank Reigen-san.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:50.180
He was working really late
last night, apparently.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:50.610
<b>Hidden Gem</b>

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:50.690
<b>Ibogami Hot Springs</b>

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:52.320
I bet he was just making those guides.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.490
<b>Hot Spring
Longevity Inn</b>

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.490
My, my...

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:01.620
Hidden Gem
Ibogami
Hot
Springs

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.410
Welcome.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.410
We've been waiting for you.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.120
I hope you had no troubles on your way here.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.000
Yeah, it went pretty smoothly.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:09.760
Oh, thank goodness. Please, come in.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.880
Wow... This is amazing.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.010
<i>It's faint, but I do feel a 
spiritual presence here.</i>

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.400
You can start your investigation 
in the morning.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.210
Please, just enjoy your stay tonight.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.020
Apparently, this inn's 
been around for a while.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:28.400
That must be why it has such 
an elegant atmosphere.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.530
A god named... Ibogami?

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.030
Oh, right.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:36.530
There used to be a hole around here
that led to another world,

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:40.160
but a god called "Ibogami-sama"
sealed it up, apparently.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:44.320
Then Ibogami-sama's devotees 
created these hot springs,

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.040
and have worshiped the god for generations.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:47.700
Huh...

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.100
This room's so pretty.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.680
Ritsu, look.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.050
Wow...

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.800
What a great view, Nii-san!

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.060
This feels so nice.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.690
Yeah. The atmosphere is great, too.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:13.300
By the way, how's the top of 
Hanazawa's head looking lately?

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:16.320
Can't see it...

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.700
N-Nii-san, apparently there's 
an outdoor bath, too.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.230
Why don't we check it out?

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.380
This is the life.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.820
No matter how much I run... It's no use...

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.510
It definitely seems to be some kind of loop.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.700
You seem calm, all things 
considered, Serizawa...

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:02.830
I was a shut-in for so long that enclosed 
spaces such as this put me at ease.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.200
I see. Good, then.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.330
I wouldn't be able to concentrate 
if you started freaking out.

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.690
<i>This is really bad...</i>

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:16.420
<i>Mob's not here, and we may 
never be able to return...</i>

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:19.720
Things not to do list 3
•Keep replies short and quick.
•If your boss seems troubled,
try reaching out to them!
Just make sure you don't wound their pride.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.430
Are you troubled?

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.760
No! This is no trouble at all!

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:27.890
I'm just being careful with my investigation

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.150
so I can find the cause
and banish it forever!

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:31.860
I see.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.640
If you understand,
leave the investigating to me.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.820
You do whatever you can.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:37.740
Yes, sir.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.180
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:52.810
<i>Reigen-san and I fell asleep. 
That's how we ended up over there.</i>

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:58.290
This is our inn's renowned Ibogami 
Dinner with Ibo's bounty.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:00.380
This looks so good.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.930
Fried items: Salt-grilled Ibodai Butterfish, Baked Ibogami Village Apples, Paprika & Cucumbers, Rock Butterfish Nanbanzuke
Hot Pot: Local Chicken, Tofu, Shungiku, Nagaibo, White Ibo, and White Maitake Hot Pot
Stewed Items: Koya Tofu, Carrots, Ibo, and Herring; Konbu-wrapped Butterfish
Sashimi: Butterfish Sashimi
Soup: Soup with Ibo Meatballs

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.930
Everything's got Ibo-something...

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:04.500
Please enjoy your meal.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.020
Ah, Serizawa-san.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:12.190
Wow, that all looks delicious. I'm starving.

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.440
Let's eat.

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:19.510
Man, and here I thought
it was a juicy deal...

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:21.300
Why is this happening to me?

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:24.990
Should that jerk be sleeping right now?

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:28.700
He was doing his best, so I thought 
I probably shouldn't wake him up.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:31.180
Reigen-san is such a hard worker.

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:33.170
Yes, I agree.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:37.260
Wow, Ibo-style deer sashimi?

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:40.040
Nii-san, have you tried this yet?

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:42.150
Ibogami-style baked apples, apparently.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.390
They're so juicy!

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.370
This salt-grilled Ibodai butterfish 
is also plump and delicious.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.270
<i>So this is all the food I have on hand...</i>

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.730
<b>Gurrrrgle</b>

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:03.410
Oh, Serizawa. How'd it go?

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:05.910
Well, it was really delicious!

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:08.230
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:11.330
I'm asking if you figured anything out.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.630
S-Sorry about that!

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:19.210
It appears that you and I were taken into 
this dimension because we fell asleep.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:20.930
I knew it.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.680
Anything else?

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:27.530
Well, this is giving me a nostalgia trip
because it's straight out of a retro game.

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:32.030
I first saw this in a single-screen game
featuring a pair of plumbers.

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:34.100
Many moons later,

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:37.890
it made a reappearance
in a classic RPG's dungeon.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:41.480
I think that was gaming's heyday,
and the best days of my life.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:44.150
These days, it's just...

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:47.240
Yeah, yeah, I got it. Don't say any more.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.470
Anyway, this is your share.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:52.540
Right... Thank you very much.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.220
Make sure you eat that sparingly.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:58.260
Something tells me we've already 
been here for over two days.

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:02.550
At this rate, we may starve to death... 
Granted, I'd never let that happen.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.400
But just in case.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.100
I'm going to go take a bath.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.840
He's starting to lose it.

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:22.910
Hot springs are the best.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:29.140
Wow.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:32.240
What the hell?

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.560
What was he even going to do with this?

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.710
<b>Mobpis</b>

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:37.710
<i>Here, have this.</i>

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.420
<i>For you, because you're always
doing your best!</i>

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.550
Capybara Baby Born

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:43.900
By the way, Kageyama-kun, 
do you have anyone you like?

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:45.490
<i>A baby capybara was born at 
a zoo in Seasoning City.</i>

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:47.450
Maybe someone from your class,
or maybe your club?

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:50.820
<i>Many families came to see 
the cute little critter.</i>

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.280
Om, om, om...

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:48.510
<b>Om
Om
Om</b>

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:52.350
There's no need to be embarrassed.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:54.130
<i>Capybaras are giant rodents 
that live in the Amazon,</i>

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.260
Oh, right.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:57.290
Someone from Salt Middle dropped by
Reigen-san's office the other day.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:57.990
<i>and the sex of the babies cannot be determined 
until they're about three months old.</i>

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:58.870
I'm pretty sure her name was...

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:00.110
<i>This one seems to be a 
bit larger than average.</i>

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:01.270
So, what about you, Serizawa-san?!

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.690
Huh, m-me?!

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:07.740
The only woman I've talked to in the 
last twenty years is my mother.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:09.080
<i>Since capybaras don't 
handle the cold very well,</i>

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:09.330
I'm so sorry about this.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:13.150
<i>the booth where they're on display 
has a heater and heated floors,</i>

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:17.410
<b>Om
Om
Om</b>

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:14.260
Why's a middle schooler asking a 29-year-old
 that question? For crying out loud...

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:17.410
<i>and the room is set to maintain a 
temperature of 15 degrees Celsius...</i>

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:17.070
I'm screwed...

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:21.380
Guess I've gotta go for my last resort.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:33.070
Hey, this doesn't seem so bad...

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:51.780
You can't be serious!

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.250
IIII IIII IIII IIII IIII III

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.250
|

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.250
|

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.250
|

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.250
|

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.250
